          <Pad Id="oqU12hSaCp9mNbsDKXb1XO" Bounds="85,990,830,122" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- Anchors and Out Handles are shared by the three curves: change them once and all follow. Only the In Handles (and Handle Modes) differ.&#xD;&#xA;- Handles are relative to their anchor, in units. Handle Modes is applied cyclically per anchor, an empty Spread means Free for all anchors.&#xD;&#xA;- Mirrored ignores In Handles, Aligned takes only their length. Here they hold the handles the mode produces, so the circles show what the curve really uses.&#xD;&#xA;- Closed uses all four anchors with both handles. An open curve ignores the In handle of the first and the Out handle of the last anchor.&#xD;&#xA;- The curve is one exact cubic per segment inside a QtPath, drawn with Path [Qt.Elements]. A path must fit one command to Qt (about 65 000 bytes), see HowTo Draw a Path.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl"><Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" /></p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
        </Canvas>
